\section{Introduction}
Extremaduran (\emph{estreme\~nu}, ISO 639-3 \texttt{ext}) is an endangered Romance variety of western Spain. Search results showed some orthographic, grammatical and lexicographic work but nothing on classroom teaching or textbooks. Its status as a language rather than a dialect, and its lack of settled spelling rules, are disputed.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No school textbooks or teaching programmes were found in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Overview of Extremaduran, with its orthography and grammar references: \url{https://omniglot.com/writing/extremaduran.htm}
\item Swarthmore linguistics wiki page on Extremaduran, which lists grammar explanations: \url{https://wikis.swarthmore.edu/ling073/Extremaduran}
\item University of Extremadura research-publication record: \url{https://opendata.unex.es/investiga/publicaciones/2018-202}
\item Dialnet article (PDF) on the language: \url{https://dialnet.unirioja.es/descarga/articulo/2243196.pdf}
\end{itemize}
Titles mentioned in search summaries but not seen as direct links: \emph{Ortograf\'ia del Extreme\~no} (Ismael Carmona Garc\'ia, 2017), \emph{Primera Gram\'atica Ehtreme\~na} (Pablo Gonz\'alvez, 1995), and the online \emph{Izionariu} dictionary with \emph{Gram\'atica brevi} (2004). These need verification.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
The monitoring body OSCEC is mentioned in search summaries as working on standardisation; no URL for it was found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Extremaduran Wikipedia: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremaduran_Wikipedia}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The Mercator research page on Extremaduran in Spain gives the legal and educational context: \url{https://wiki.mercator-research.eu/languages:extremaduran_in_spain}. Speaker estimates vary widely and use is concentrated among older adults, so any curriculum would start from a small base of standardised materials.

\end{document}
